# 2026-11-02 02:25:49.369513
+Please complete the remaining features for our concurrent ticket booking system in Go following clean architecture principles:
+
+1. Status Constants & Time Types:
+   - In `internals/domain.go`, define status constants: StatusHeld = "HELD", StatusBooked = "BOOKED", StatusConfirmed = "CONFIRMED", StatusReleased = "RELEASED".
+   - Change `ExpiresAt` from string to `time.Time`.
+
+2. Unique ID & Input Validation:
+   - In `internals/memory_store.go` (or domain), auto-generate a unique ID (e.g., using Google UUID or a secure random string) when a booking/hold is created.
+   - In `internals/handler.go` (`handleBookSeat`), add strict input validation: return 400 Bad Request if `movie_id`, `seat_id`, or `user_id` are empty.
+
+3. Hold-Confirm-Release Flow:
+   - Implement the full lifecycle in `BookingStore` interface and `MemoryStore`:
+     - Hold: Temporarily block a seat with an expiry time (e.g., 5 minutes).
+     - Confirm: Change status from HELD to CONFIRMED or BOOKED.
+     - Release: Free up the seat if expired or cancelled.
+
+4. Documentation & Hygiene:
+   - Create a clean `.gitignore` file for Go binaries and temporary files.
+   - Write a professional `README.md` detailing the project architecture, concurrency model (`sync.RWMutex`), API endpoints, and instructions to run tests with `go test -race`.

